PostGIS 3.3.7: where its source is, and a written offer of it
==============================================================

This image carries the binaries of PostGIS 3.3.7: the extensions postgis, postgis_raster,
postgis_sfcgal, postgis_tiger_geocoder and postgis_topology. PostGIS is licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or later. Its licence is in this folder (COPYING, LICENSE.TXT).

The binaries come unmodified from the base image supabase/postgres:17.6.1.175. Aber does not
modify or rebuild them, and Aber's migrations do not create these extensions. This applies to the
three images built on that base: ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/supabase-db,
ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/db-init and ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/backup-service.


Where the source is
-------------------

- PostGIS 3.3.7, with no patches:
  https://github.com/postgis/postgis/tree/3.3.7
  The base image was built from its release archive,
  https://download.osgeo.org/postgis/source/postgis-3.3.7.tar.gz
- The scripts that built it, in supabase/postgres at 17.6.1.175 (nix/ext/postgis.nix and
  nix/ext/gdal.nix):
  https://github.com/supabase/postgres/tree/17.6.1.175
  and the nixpkgs its flake.lock pins, which builds the libraries below:
  https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/tree/fb7944c166a3b630f177938e478f0378e64ce108


The copyleft libraries only PostGIS loads
-----------------------------------------

PostGIS's modules load these libraries, which the PostgreSQL server does not. Each is in the
image's Nix store, unmodified, and its licence is under /usr/share/licenses/<name>/.

- GEOS 3.14.1, GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 (geos/):
  https://github.com/libgeos/geos/tree/3.14.1
- SFCGAL 2.2.0, GNU Library General Public License 2 or later (sfcgal/):
  https://gitlab.com/sfcgal/SFCGAL/-/tree/v2.2.0
- CGAL 6.1, compiled into SFCGAL (cgal/):
  https://github.com/CGAL/cgal/tree/v6.1
  The SFCGAL library carries CGAL packages under the GNU General Public License 3 or later
  (Nef_3, Straight_skeleton_2, Minkowski_sum_2, Minkowski_sum_3, Polygon_mesh_processing,
  Triangulation_2, Triangulation_3, Alpha_shapes_2, Convex_hull_3, Polyhedron, Surface_mesh,
  Arrangement_on_surface_2, Boolean_set_operations_2, Polyline_simplification_2,
  Box_intersection_d and AABB_tree), and its kernel and support packages under the GNU Lesser
  General Public License 3 or later. The SFCGAL library in this image is therefore under the GNU
  General Public License 3 or later.
- GMP 6.3.0, GNU Lesser General Public License 3 or later, or GNU General Public License 2 or
  later (gmp/):
  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
- MPFR 4.2.2, GNU Lesser General Public License 3 or later (mpfr/):
  https://gitlab.inria.fr/mpfr/mpfr/-/tree/4.2.2
- libidn2 2.3.8, GNU General Public License 2 or later, or GNU Lesser General Public License 3
  or later (libidn2/):
  https://gitlab.com/libidn/libidn2/-/tree/v2.3.8
- libunistring 1.4.1, GNU Lesser General Public License 3 or later, or GNU General Public
  License 2 or later (libunistring/):
  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libunistring/libunistring-1.4.1.tar.gz


The written offer
-----------------

For three years from the date of each Aber release that ships this image, Aber's maintainer will
give anyone who asks a complete machine-readable copy of the corresponding source code of the
binaries above: PostGIS 3.3.7 and the libraries listed here, with the scripts that built them.
The charge is no more than the cost of making the copy.

To ask, use GitHub's private vulnerability reporting for Aber:
https://github.com/Harri-Llewelyn/Aber/security/advisories/new
(the Security tab, then Report a vulnerability). The form is built for vulnerability reports.
Use it for a source request too. Say in it:

- which image you have and its tag, the Aber release (for example
  ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/supabase-db);
- that this is a request for the GPL source of PostGIS.

The request opens a draft advisory that only Aber's maintainers can see.
